[Part D] exponent bookkeeping (CMP 119 (2.31), (2.43)-(2.46), (3.67)); n-j = s
   per point z of the j-lattice the remainder after the counterterm is O((L^-s)^(5-b)) (3.67),
   the F^2 term itself O((L^-s)^4) (3.57)-(3.66); the number of z per unit n-cell is L^(s d).
   d=4: summed remainder exponent 5-d-b = 1-b; summed F^2 (marginal) exponent 4-d = 0
   d=3: summed remainder exponent 5-d-b = 2-b (only with a counterterm, absent at d = 3); summed F^2 (marginal) exponent 4-d = 1
   d=4, L=2: sum_(s=0..60) L^(-(4-d)s) = 61.000000   (limit n->inf: inf)
   d=3, L=2: sum_(s=0..60) L^(-(4-d)s) = 2.000000   (limit n->inf: 2.0)
   d=3, L=3: sum_(s=0..60) L^(-(4-d)s) = 1.500000   (limit n->inf: 1.4999999999999998)
   d=4, L=2: L^d - 1 = 15 non-central sites per block; d^2 = 16
   d=3, L=2: L^d - 1 = 7 non-central sites per block; d^2 = 9
   d=3, L=3: L^d - 1 = 26 non-central sites per block; d^2 = 9
   => d=4: the marginal sum grows like n (needs the beta_j counterterm and g_j^kappa0 factors);
      d=3: it is a convergent geometric series, no coupling counterterm is needed, (2.43) holds with exponent 1 (beta = 1 in (2.43)'s own notation).

