[Part F] (i) exp(-c p_0(g)^2) <= (g p_0(g))^q for lam = log g^-2 >= lam_*(q);
   p_0(g) = A_0 lam^p0 (CMP 119 p. 244; p. 246 text after (1.1)), g = exp(-lam/2). Take A_0 = 1 (A_0 >= 1 only helps).
   Condition: c lam^(2 p0) >= q (lam/2 - p0 ln lam).  Sufficient: c lam^(2 p0) >= q lam/2,
   i.e. lam >= (q/(2c))^(1/(2 p0 - 1)) (and lam >= 1).  lam_* below = last sign change of the exact condition on a grid of step 1e-3.
     c=0.5, p0=10, q=5: lam_* = 1.034 (g^2 <= 3.556e-01); sufficient closed form lam >= 1.088; closed form >= lam_*: True
